{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":85318,"duration_api_ms":123335,"num_turns":6,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9aa2a915-8801-4a74-bae0-6e6de6a6262c","total_cost_usd":0.5581829,"usage":{"input_tokens":1233,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26607,"cache_read_input_tokens":79201,"output_tokens":2584,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26607,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":54,"outputTokens":3987,"cacheReadInputTokens":148299,"cacheCreationInputTokens":25044,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0661239,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":1241,"outputTokens":3994,"cacheReadInputTokens":199658,"cacheCreationInputTokens":45788,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.492059,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Accept three amendments with verified correctness/maintainability issues (default placeholder, photoperiod test coupling, substrate factor split source of truth). Reject the reproduction baseline amendment because the test passes on the current tree — the claimed failure is unsubstantiated.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-5ed4a8bc","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: `SubstrateLayerState::default()` hardcodes `colonizable_area_cm2: 100.0` (substrate.rs:56), but the derived value for default geometry (40×25=1000 cm², InertSand factor 0.5, 3cm depth) is 1500.0 — a 15× discrepancy. Although `TankState::new()` and `refresh_habitat_registry()` both overwrite this, any code path that reads the default before engine initialization gets a silently wrong value. Setting it to `0.0` or computing it from defaults would make stale reads immediately obvious. This is a genuine correctness footgun."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-211b5df3","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: The test comment says 'hours 0-7 are lit' and branches on `hour < 8` for lit_peak, but `is_light_on()` centers the photoperiod on noon — its own unit test confirms the actual lit hours for 8h photoperiod are [8,9,10,11,12,13,14,15]. The test is therefore sampling the wrong bucket (dark hours as lit, lit hours ignored). Even if the test happens to pass by coincidence of current DO values, the logic is objectively wrong and brittle. Deriving lit/dark from `is_light_on()` is the correct fix."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-fce9ecb0","decision":"reject","rationale":"The claimed failure is not reproducible. Running `cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_baseline_scenarios maintained_medium_variant_reaches_reproduction_window` on the current tree shows the test passes, including all three day-envelope checks (repro_day30/60/90) and the final reproduction_window assertion. Without evidence of an actual failure, loosening the asserted bands would weaken a functioning regression gate for no demonstrated benefit."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-24f6329b","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: `SubstratePreset` defines `colonizable_area_factor` (presets.rs:229), but `tank_scenarios/lib.rs` only maps the preset ID to a `SubstrateKind` enum variant. All downstream computation in `derived_colonizable_area_cm2()` uses `SubstrateKind::colonizable_area_factor()` which returns hard-coded values (0.5/0.6/0.8/0.9). The code itself acknowledges this with a comment: 'Keep these values aligned with the substrate preset pack until the factor is promoted into first-class serialized layer metadata.' This is a genuine split source of truth — preset changes to the factor are silently ignored."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"9fc0f7be-453e-4035-9474-3f1195a9d314"}
